 {:surface :interval,
  :key "SELECT ARRAY['00:00:00'::interval]::text",
  :reason
  "CACHE COLLISION: the ARRAY path returns a cmp-equal but DIFFERENT carrier -- `array['1 mon'::interval]` renders as `{\"30 days\"}`, and in a fresh session `array['00:00:00'::interval]` gave `{\"1 mon -30 days\"}`. The answer depends on what ran earlier in the session, so a query form containing the folded carrier is being cached under a key that treats cmp-equal intervals as the same query. arrays.clj itself is correct in isolation. Same class as the datahike BigDecimal-scale collision: any cache keyed on =-but-not-identical values collides. Needs its own fix -- the carrier must not appear in a cache key."}
